# Origin-workspace detail that must never appear in any file this repo SHIPS.
#
# One extended-regex alternation per line; `#` comments and blank lines ignored. Read by the
# "no origin-workspace detail" gate in tests/run-all.sh, which scans EVERY FILE THAT WOULD SHIP
# (computed from .gitignore) and skips only this file — the one place these strings are
# supposed to exist. Local-only files (whatever .gitignore's publish-time block lists) are not scanned: they don't ship.
#
# WHY EVERYTHING THAT SHIPS, NOT JUST THE PAYLOAD. Until 2026-07-28 the gate scanned only
# references/ skills/ scripts/ README.md .claude-plugin/, and `tests/` was deliberately exempt.
# That exemption WAS the publish blocker: the multi-repo oracle was a real private workspace's
# index and the grader hardcoded its repo names, so the repo could not go public. With those
# rebuilt against tests/fixtures/layer2-chain/, nothing needs the exemption, and a gate that
# covers everything is the only version that keeps it closed.
#
# Adding a name here is cheap. Do it whenever a real workspace's detail could plausibly get
# pasted in.
#
# ⚠️ MEASUREMENT TRAP, cost an hour on 2026-07-28. Do NOT hand-verify this gate by typing a
# `grep` into an interactive Claude Code / zsh session: `grep` there is a shell FUNCTION that
# respects .gitignore, so it silently reports gitignored paths as clean. Inside a bash script
# — which is how run-all.sh runs — `grep` is /usr/bin/grep, which does not. The gate is
# therefore honest and the ad-hoc check is not, which is the dangerous way round. To verify by
# hand, call `/usr/bin/grep` explicitly, or just run `bash tests/run-all.sh`.
invoiceapp
invoice-backend
invoice-frontend
invoice-reports
supabase
stripe
paynow
/Users/
